extends ../layout-marketing

block vars
	- metadata = {title: 'Help'}
	- isWebsiteRedesign = true

block content
	main#main-content.content
		.container
			.row
				.col-lg-8.offset-lg-2
					h1 Help
					p
						| #{settings.appName} is the Institute's collaborative LaTeX editor. This page covers the platform itself; for LaTeX, start with the guides below.

					h2.h3#visual-editor Editing without knowing LaTeX
					ul
						li
							| Choose
							|
							strong Visual
							|
							| above the editor to edit headings, lists, bold and italic text, tables and figures as they look, rather than as code. The PDF on the right follows when you recompile.
						li
							strong Format › Page setup
							|
							| (also the line-spacing button at the start of the toolbar) changes the font size, line spacing (single, 1.5 or double), margins, paper size and font of the whole document, and recompiles. It works in the main file, the one that starts with
							|
							code \documentclass
							| .
						li
							strong Insert › IIT Mandi logo
							|
							| puts the Institute logo where the cursor is. New blank projects already show it at the top; delete those lines if you don't need it.
						li
							| To find where something in the PDF comes from, double-click it in the PDF: the editor jumps to that place.
						li
							| Undo (Ctrl+Z) takes back the last changes, and
							|
							strong History
							|
							| restores any earlier version.

					h2.h3 Learning LaTeX
					ul
						li
							a(href='https://www.learnlatex.org/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') Learn LaTeX
							|  — short lessons for beginners, with examples to try.
						li
							a(href='https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/LaTeX' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') LaTeX Wikibook
							|  — a reference for document structure, tables, figures, mathematics and bibliographies.
						li
							a(href='https://ctan.org/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') CTAN
							|  — the documentation of every LaTeX package.

					h2.h3 Fixing compile errors
					ul
						li
							| The logs next to the PDF list each error with the line that caused it. Fix the first error first: the ones after it often follow from it.
						li
							| For an unfamiliar message, search
							|
							a(href='https://tex.stackexchange.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer') TeX Stack Exchange
							| .
						li
							| If the PDF stops updating or looks out of date, choose
							|
							strong Recompile from scratch
							|
							| in the Recompile menu.
						li
							| When many people compile at the same time, your compile waits for a free slot and starts on its own.

					h2.h3#compile-time Long documents and compile time
					ul
						li
							| Every compile has a time limit.
							if settings.compileQueue && settings.compileQueue.turnMs
								|
								| While others are waiting, a long compile pauses every #{Math.round(settings.compileQueue.turnMs / 1000)} seconds and carries on when a slot is free, so a thesis still compiles when the server is busy. Time spent paused does not count towards the limit.
						li
							| When a compile reaches its limit, or you stop it, the PDF shows the pages typeset up to that point. The next compile reuses the files it left behind, so it is usually faster.
						li
							| LaTeX typesets the whole document in every compile, but it does not have to draw every picture again. Load
							|
							code \usepackage[extract=tex]{memoize}
							|
							| before TikZ or pgfplots: each picture is then drawn once and reused until you change it. In our test, a document with eight plots went from 78 seconds for the first compile to 3 seconds for the next ones.
						li
							| For a thesis, put each chapter in its own file and load it with
							|
							code \include{chapter3}
							| . While you work on one chapter, add
							|
							code \includeonly{chapter3}
							|
							| to the preamble: only that chapter is typeset, and its page numbers and references to other chapters stay correct.
						li
							| The
							|
							strong Fast [draft]
							|
							| compile mode in the Recompile menu leaves out images while you write.
						li
							| Large images slow every compile down: scale them to the size at which they are printed.

					h2.h3 Sharing and collaborating
					ul
						li
							| Use
							|
							strong Share
							|
							if settings.shareLinksCanEdit === false
								| in the editor to invite people by their IIT Mandi email address as viewers or editors, or to turn on a view-only link. Nobody can edit a project unless its owner invited them by name.
							else
								| in the editor to invite people by their IIT Mandi email address, or to turn on view-only and edit links.
						li
							| Shared projects and links open only after logging in with an IIT Mandi account.
						li
							strong History
							|
							| shows every change to a project and can restore earlier versions.

					h2.h3 Projects
					ul
						li
							| Archiving a project hides it from your project list without deleting it.
						if settings.retention && settings.retention.trashDays > 0
							li
								| Projects you own are deleted #{settings.retention.trashDays} days after you move them to the trash, so take back anything you still need before then.
						li
							| A project you delete from the trash cannot be restored by you. An administrator can recover it for #{Math.round(settings.projectHardDeletionDelay / 86400000)} days; after that it is removed for good.

					if settings.storageQuota && settings.storageQuota.defaultMB > 0
						h2.h3#storage Storage space
						ul
							li
								| Each account has #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB for the files and documents in the projects it owns, including archived projects and projects in the trash. Projects shared with you count towards their owner's space, not yours.
							if settings.storageQuota.maxMB > settings.storageQuota.defaultMB
								li
									| Those #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB are always yours, and you are not stopped there: while the server has room, you can use up to #{settings.storageQuota.maxMB} MB. If the server runs low on space, people using more than #{settings.storageQuota.defaultMB} MB are asked to free some before adding files.
							li
								| The project list and your account settings show how much you are using, and the settings list your largest projects. Earlier versions kept in a project's history don't count.
							li
								| To free space, delete files you no longer need, or delete old projects from the trash.
							li
								| If your work needs more space, for example a thesis with many images, write to
								|
								a(href='mailto:' + settings.adminEmail) #{settings.adminEmail}
								| .

					if settings.askAi && settings.askAi.url
						h2.h3#ask-ai Ask AI
						ul
							li
								strong Ask AI
								|
								| in the editor toolbar opens #{settings.askAi.name} in a window beside the editor, with the text you selected. The sparkle button on a compile error asks it what causes the error and how to fix it.
							li
								| #{settings.askAi.name} is an outside service, not part of #{settings.appName}. You use it with your own account, and what you send goes to its provider, so leave out anything confidential.
							li
								| To see both at once, move the editor window to the left half of your screen.

					if settings.editorPlaces && settings.editorPlaces.limit > 0
						h2.h3#editor-waiting-room When the editor is full
						ul
							li
								if settings.editorPlaces.maxLimit > settings.editorPlaces.limit
									| To keep editing fast for everyone, the number of people who can have the editor open at once depends on how busy the server is: at least #{settings.editorPlaces.limit}, and up to #{settings.editorPlaces.maxLimit} while it has room.
								else
									| To keep editing fast for everyone, at most #{settings.editorPlaces.limit} people can have the editor open at the same time.
							li
								| When it is full, opening a project shows your place in the queue. Keep that tab open: the project opens by itself as soon as a place is free.
							li
								| After #{settings.editorPlaces.idleMinutes} minutes without typing, clicking or scrolling, your place goes to the next person waiting. When you come back, you get a free place again, or a place in the queue.

					h2.h3 Git
					p
						| You can clone, pull and push projects with git. Create an authentication token in your account settings, and use it as the password when git asks for one.

					h2.h3 Browsers
					p
						| Use a version of Chrome, Firefox, Safari or Edge released in the last year. Older browsers, and Internet Explorer, are not supported.

					h2.h3 Contact
					p
						| For questions, problems with your account or anything this page doesn't answer, write to
						|
						a(href='mailto:' + settings.adminEmail) #{settings.adminEmail}
						| .
